#     https://github.com/8devices/openwrt-8devices.git
#   cd openwrt-8devices && git sparse-checkout set package/kernel/rtl8192cd
#   patch -p1 < g3-rtl8192cd-4.14-port.patch
#
# OTHER LOAD-BEARING POINTS
# - The BSP_* wall was UNREACHABLE DEAD CODE (CONFIG_RTL_819X never defined).
# - <asm/uaccess.h> -> <linux/uaccess.h> in 14 files: 55 -> 101 objects.
# - CONFIG_BAND_2G_ON_WLAN0 is essential: without it wlan_device[] degenerates to
#   all-zero TYPE_PCI_BIOS entries and the embedded radio is never touched.
# - ★★ 8822BE support MUST stay compiled out or this driver steals PCI 10ec:b822
#   from rtw88 and kills the 5 GHz AP. CONFIG_PCI_HCI stays ON.
# - Path B (WEXT): RTK_NL80211 / CONFIG_OPENWRT_SDK off. Stock is Path B too.
# - 8192cd_owrt_bsp.c supplies the two Realtek-BSP exports this tree lacks;
#   PCIE_reset_procedure_97F() is a deliberate read-only stub (the real one drives
#   PERST# low for 300ms and would drop the bus rtw88 lives on).
# - ⚠ 'make modules' alone SILENTLY SKIPS undefined-symbol checks without vmlinux.
#
